  "verbalization": "Ixerisoside A appears to interact with DNMT3A2/3L complex through a multi-step pathway, with the final target being the DNMT3A2/3L complex itself. The evidence suggests that Ixerisoside A acts as a target for Chloramphenicol acetyltransferase, which in turn is a target of Galacturonic Acid and another compound, (1S,4R,7R)-5-methyl-7-[(2S)-6-methylhept-5-en-2-yl]-2,3-dioxabicyclo[2.2.2]oct-5-ene. This chain of targets ultimately leads to the DNMT3A2/3L complex, indicating a potential regulatory or enzymatic pathway involving these molecules. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Ixerisoside A in modulating DNMT3A2/3L activity through the activation of downstream targets. The evidence supports a mechanism where Ixerisoside A may influence DNMT3A2/3L complex function via a series of intermediate compounds, suggesting a complex, multi-target interaction network.",
